  "articleBody": "Thinking about whether it's time to give your living room lighting an overhaul? There are usually no legal deadlines for home lighting improvements, but addressing inadequate light is a smart move for safety and comfort. Here are some signs it's probably time to call in a professional to help with an upgrade: \n\n*   **You're constantly fumbling for switches in the dark.** If getting from your sofa to the door involves feeling your way around, your lighting isn't doing its job. \n*   **The room has noticeable dark spots or corners.** Uneven lighting can be frustrating and even create tripping hazards. You want uniform illumination. \n*   **You're experiencing glare from existing fixtures.** Sometimes, the issue isn't too little light, but light that's poorly directed or too harsh, reflecting off surfaces. \n*   **It's hard to read or do detailed tasks in the room.** If you're squinting to read a book, your ambient or task lighting is insufficient. \n*   **You rely on just one or two lamps for the entire room.** This often leads to a room that feels dim and doesn't utilize the space effectively. \n\nWhen you're looking at adding new circuits, installing dimmers, or putting in hardwired lights, that's when a licensed electrician becomes essential. HH Remodeling LLC, serving the greater Denver area, can help identify your lighting needs and coordinate with trusted sub-trades to ensure your living room lighting is both functional and beautiful.",
  "datePublished": "2026-08-09"
